4,Mbangala language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/mbangala_language,"Mbangala, also known as Umbangala or Cimbangala, is a Bantu language of the Niger-Congo family, classified under Guthrie zone H.34 and spoken primarily by the Mbangala people in the northeastern provinces of Angola, including Malanje, Lunda Norte, and Lunda Sul.",Mbangala,Niger-Congo
